---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="FAQ | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="Practical answers about working with Saielle DaSilva: sliding scale, engagements, sessions, speaking logistics and payment."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
      <h1>Fair questions.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Straight answers about rates, sliding scale and how engagements
        actually run. Anything missing: ask me.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="faq">
      <section>
        <h2>How does the sliding scale work?</h2>
        <p>
          Ask. If cost is the thing standing between you and booking, say so
          in your note. It counts if you are paying yourself rather than an
          employer, if your company is bootstrapped or unfunded, if the work
          is for a charity, nonprofit or the public sector, or if the full
          rate simply means you would not book at all.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no proof to send, no essay to write and no negotiation.
          I will confirm an adjusted rate when we book. A few reduced slots
          each month keeps this honest; if the month is full, I will tell
          you and we will find another way.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What happens after I get in touch?</h2>
        <p>
          I reply to every serious note, usually within a couple of working
          days. We book a short call to scope things. If it looks like a
          fit, you get a brief written proposal: what we would do, when,
          and what it costs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>What happens in a strategy session?</h2>
        <p>
          Beforehand you answer a few questions, so the clock starts on
          substance rather than introductions. Then ninety minutes working
          your actual problem. Afterwards you get written notes: decisions
          made, next steps, who owns what.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Is fractional leadership a real commitment?</h2>
        <p>
          Yes, and that is the point. Fractional work runs on an agreed
          rhythm over months, not days. Quick rescue thoughts are exactly
          what strategy sessions are for; fractional leadership is for
          teams that want direction held steady while they build.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Do you speak virtually?</h2>
        <p>
          Yes. Remote keynotes and workshops carry the same fee unless the
          format is much shorter. For in-person events, travel and
          accommodation are covered by the organizer.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Will you sign an NDA?</h2>
        <p>Happily. Send yours, or use mine.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Can I hire you full-time?</h2>
        <p>
          For the right role, yes. Director level and above. The same
          clarity principle applies: shared understanding of the goal before
          we commit. If that sounds like your team, write me a note and
          tell me what you are trying to accomplish.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>How does payment work?</h2>
        <p>
          Invoice and bank transfer, GBP unless we agree otherwise. Terms
          are on every proposal; nothing surprising arrives later.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2>Something else?</h2>
        <p>
          Ask me directly:
          <a href="mailto:hello@intentionaut.com">hello@intentionaut.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
